      "learn": {
        "text": "Factors are numbers that divide exactly into a number. Factors of 12: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12 (they come in pairs: 1×12, 2×6, 3×4). Multiples are in a number's times table: multiples of 4 are 4, 8, 12... A prime number has exactly two factors: 1 and itself.",
